attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a potassium-transporting spine.** Columns 0 to 5, `kdpF` to `kdpE`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 5% of calls {S1}. The model names 95 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 3, `kdpC`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **A fork opens at column 6**, `speFL`, carried by 78%, with a "TonB-dependent receptor" at 31% and an "IS1 family transposase" at 26% {S2.c6}. The stretch most in regions of plasticity is columns 6 to 10, RGP 45 to 76%, [[potassium transport]] {S2, P, Q}. Then the `nag` genes, columns 21 to 25, [[glucosamine phosphate]] {S5, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 86%, and hesitates less there, 0.17 against 0.38 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 6, `speFL`, a fork column, 1.17 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a fork.** Columns 78 to 79, `rnk` and `uspG`, are carried by 89 and 57% of chromosomes, all persistent {S14}. The last column is `uspG`, in 57% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.22 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.70 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 70% against 96% {C}.

